  "answer": "A technical support answer must add the qualification that precise, page-level PDF citations are **highly dependent on document quality** [NL-002#NL-002-S09]; for **image-only, scanned, or low-quality PDFs**, the system must rely on OCR, and if the scan is low quality or misaligned, the OCR parser may produce broken or incomplete text blocks, leading to **missing citations, incorrect page links, or TutorChat stating it cannot find the answer** [NL-002#NL-002-S09]. Specifically, for low-quality scans the system may struggle to generate page-specific citations, so support should recommend checking scan quality or re-saving the document in a digital text-searchable format [NL-028#NL-028-S03]. Additionally, technical support must clarify that such files may yield citations that point to the entire document or page 1 of a larger file rather than the exact section [NL-006#NL-006-S04][NL-011#NL-011-S05].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
